Linux Commands Documentation

Environment

- Cloud Provider: AWS
- Service: EC2
- Operating System: Ubuntu Linux
- Access Method: SSH

File Management Commands

Command| Purpose
"ls"| List files and directories
"pwd"| Display current directory
"cd"| Change directory
"mkdir"| Create a directory
"touch"| Create a file
"cat"| Display file content
"echo"| Write text to a file
"cp"| Copy files
"mv"| Move or rename files
"chmod"| Modify file permissions
"ls -l"| View file permissions and ownership

System Administration

Command| Purpose
"whoami"| Display current user
"ps aux"| View running processes
"top"| Monitor system processes
"systemctl status"| Check service status
"ip addr"| View network interfaces
"hostname -I"| Display private IP address
"ss -tuln"| View listening ports

Learning Outcome

Developed practical knowledge of Linux command-line operations, file management, permissions, and basic server administration.
